@startuml uc-migrate-configuration
!include _theme.iuml

state migrateConfiguration as "migrateConfiguration()" {

  state " " as RequestingConversion
  state " " as Previewing
  state " " as Deciding

  [*] --> RequestingConversion
  note on link
  <b>Policy author</b> asks to convert a file that names its
  account in a root owner field
  end note

  RequestingConversion --> Previewing
  note on link
  <b>Octoform</b> resolves the document and reports what it is
  • a file that already declares owners needs no migration
  • the converted result is equivalent: the same repositories
    resolve to the same policy
  end note

  Previewing --> Deciding
  note on link
  <b>Octoform</b> prints the converted document and changes
  nothing, because previewing is the default
  end note

  Deciding --> [*]
  note on link
  <b>Policy author</b> either keeps the preview, or asks for
  --write to convert the file in place
  end note
}

migrateConfiguration --> CONFIGURATION_RESOLVED
note on link
comments, ordering and formatting survive:
the conversion moves blocks rather than
re-serializing the document
end note

migrateConfiguration -[#A78BFA]-> CONFIGURATION_RESOLVED
note on link
--write refused: the file has uncommitted
changes in a git working tree, so the
conversion could not be reviewed as a diff
end note
@enduml
